Core's level: Aggressive · Kill switch: off

Turn the kill switch on?
Everything "Revoke all" ends, and work running now in every pane of this Corbanu Terminal stops, Claude panes included: a reply in progress is
cancelled and its commands are stopped, as when you interrupt it, and background terminals end.
Until you turn it off here: this Corbanu Terminal sends nothing to the model (each new turn is refused with a message saying so), messages and
tasks from other agents wait (a Claude pane keeps only the newest task; a task for a Corbanu pane you opened yourself in /panes is refused instead),
assignments and whips are paused, no grant can be issued, protected actions after untrusted content are refused, the browser and memory writes are
refused, and the credential broker stays closed. Another Corbanu Terminal on this home takes the switch when it next starts.
Other Corbanu Terminals running on this home take it too, within about a second: their running work stops the same way and they refuse new turns.
Saved in security_state.json: it holds after a restart. The level stays Aggressive. Turning it off later restarts nothing: work resumes only when
someone acts.

